{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Cross-epic assignment from the docs/ADR epic (astounding-pictural-cowbird): two comments in modules this story moves cite a design document (`docs/designs/sync-hardening-proposal.md`) that never existed in git history. Rewrite them in this change, at the moved paths (origin/main 083620b0 line numbers):\n\n- `inbound_differ.py:265-266`: replace `# Canonical entries (as of 183fd51ac2; pending consolidation into` / `# _field_contract.py per docs/designs/sync-hardening-proposal.md Item 3):` with `# Canonical entries (as of 183fd51ac2; the per-field symmetry rules live in` / `# _field_contract.py, which names this map; consolidation tracked by story a130-2b7c-429c-43d1):`.\n- `apply_handlers.py:504-505`: replace `evidence feeds the binding-GC design in` / `# docs/designs/sync-hardening-proposal.md Item 4b.` with `evidence feeds binding retirement per ADR 0028 (deletion is proven only by a` / `# direct 404; bug 13eb-c414-0763-4fa1 covers GC of bindings to deleted issues).`\n\nBoth replacement blocks stay accepted by `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` (grouped-hex ticket ids present). The docs epic's own story fixes the remaining phantom citations in `scripts/` and `tests/`; after both land, `git grep -n 'sync-hardening-proposal'` over `src scripts tests` is empty."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788807986691990359,"uuid":"d7739122-264d-4057-b6ba-ec7c55d9e232"}